  "id": "DrugBank_DB12459 - MONDO_5744",
  "verbalization": "Belotecan, through its indication for Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary, Maligant Granulosa Cell Tumor Of Ovary, and Ovarian Clear Cell Adenocarcinoma, is linked to Altretamine, which in turn is associated with Yolk Sac Tumor. This suggests that Belotecan may share a common mechanism of action or biological pathway with Altretamine, potentially targeting similar molecular targets or pathways in ovarian tumors. The evidence indicates that Belotecan could be a potential repurposed therapy for Yolk Sac Tumor, as it is linked through a chain of indications to a drug that is also associated with this tumor. The recurring association with Altretamine, a known agent in the treatment of Yolk Sac Tumor, supports the possibility of Belotecan being a viable candidate for re-evaluation in this context. The strength of the evidence lies in the consistent linkage through indications, suggesting a possible biological relationship that warrants further investigation.",
